TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE #1 - DOCKER PORT CONFLICT
==============================================

ISSUE
-----
Error Message:

failed to bind host port 0.0.0.0:8002
Address already in use

Meaning:

Another application or container is already using port 8002.
Docker cannot use the same port twice.


ROOT CAUSE
----------
Possible causes:

1. FastAPI/Uvicorn already running
2. Existing Docker container using port 8002
3. Another application using port 8002
4. Previous container not stopped properly


CHECK WHAT IS USING PORT 8002
-----------------------------

# show process using port 8002
sudo lsof -i :8002

OR

# show network listeners
sudo netstat -tulpn | grep 8002

Expected Output:

python
uvicorn
docker-proxy
or another PID


CHECK RUNNING CONTAINERS
------------------------

# list running containers
docker ps

Look for:

0.0.0.0:8002->8002/tcp

If found:

Container is already using port 8002.


STOP CONTAINER
--------------

# stop container
docker stop CONTAINER_ID

Example:

docker stop abc123


STOP ALL CONTAINERS
-------------------

# stop all running containers
docker stop $(docker ps -q)


REMOVE STOPPED CONTAINERS
-------------------------

# remove stopped containers
docker container prune


ALTERNATIVE SOLUTION
--------------------
Use another port.

Incorrect:

docker run -p 8003:8003 sre-copilot

Reason:

Application runs on port 8002 inside container.

Correct:

docker run -p 8003:8002 sre-copilot

Meaning:

Host Port 8003
       |
       v
Container Port 8002


VERIFY CONTAINER
----------------

# check container status
docker ps

Expected:

0.0.0.0:8003->8002/tcp


TEST APPLICATION
----------------

# test application
curl http://localhost:8003


OPEN SWAGGER UI
---------------

http://localhost:8003/docs


VMWARE USERS
------------
Find Ubuntu IP:

hostname -I

Example:

192.168.1.100

Open:

http://192.168.1.100:8003/docs


SUCCESS CASE
------------
Expected Logs:

INFO: Started server process
INFO: Application startup complete
INFO: Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8002

And Docker Mapping:

Host 8003 -> Container 8002


LESSON LEARNED
--------------
Container Port:

8002

Host Port:

Can be:
8002
8003
8004
8010
9000

Rule:

Host Port can be anything free.
Container Port must match the application port.
